    "description": "<p>A chainsaw is a portable handheld power saw that cuts with a set of teeth attached to a rotating chain driven along a guide bar. A chainsaw comprises an engine, a drive mechanism, a guide bar, a cutting chain, a tensioning mechanism, and safety features. Chainsaws are typically gasoline or electric-powered and used for tasks to cut through plants and wood and sometimes even concrete and ice, though smaller versions are used for certain surgical procedures. Chainsaws are stupendously dangerous to their operator, but those dangers make them horrifically effective weapons.</p>",
